description:
## Problem

Integration tests spawn sigild with --idle-timeout never but never call child.kill() before the test ends. On test exit or panic, the daemon is orphaned and runs forever. With many needle workers running concurrently, this produces cascading orphaned sigild processes that block all needle workers in the SIGIL workspace indefinitely.

Affected files (all spawn sigild with --idle-timeout never and no cleanup):
- crates/sigil-integration-tests/tests/daemon_startup_test.rs
- crates/sigil-integration-tests/tests/phase2_redteam_test.rs
- crates/sigil-integration-tests/tests/daemon_hardening_test.rs
- crates/sigil-integration-tests/tests/phase2_4_startup_modes_verification_test.rs
- test_startup_modes.sh

## Fix

Add a DaemonGuard RAII struct to the integration test helpers that kills the child on Drop. Replace every bare spawn() result with DaemonGuard::new(child).

### 1. Add DaemonGuard to crates/sigil-integration-tests/src/lib.rs

    pub struct DaemonGuard(std::process::Child);

    impl DaemonGuard {
        pub fn new(child: std::process::Child) -> Self { Self(child) }
    }

    impl Drop for DaemonGuard {
        fn drop(&mut self) {
            let _ = self.0.kill();
            let _ = self.0.wait();
        }
    }

### 2. In each affected test, wrap the child:

    // Before (leaks daemon):
    let mut child = Command::new(&sigild)
        .arg("start").arg("--idle-timeout").arg("never")
        .spawn().expect("Failed to start daemon");

    // After (daemon killed on drop, even on panic):
    let _guard = DaemonGuard::new(
        Command::new(&sigild)
            .arg("start").arg("--idle-timeout").arg("never")
            .spawn().expect("Failed to start daemon")
    );

## Acceptance

- cargo test -p sigil-integration-tests completes with no lingering sigild processes
- pgrep sigild returns empty immediately after the test suite exits
- All existing test assertions still pass (kill happens after test body, not during)
- Commit and push
